{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/standardcontext\/vendoridentifierkey"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"VendorIdentifierKey"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The system gives the same identifier to every app of one vendor on one device, and a new one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once all of them are removed. Traffluent reads it and never stores it, nor makes one up where","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the system has none: on macOS and Linux, and on a device whose system hasn’t one yet (just","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"restarted, still locked), records carry no key. It is a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value, so a destination","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads it only through the record it arrived in, and not at all once a delivery redacts it:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let vendorID = record.context[VendorIdentifierKey.self].flatMap(record.reveal)  \/\/ a UUID"],"type":"codeListing"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ServiceContext"},{"text":" key of the platform’s identifier for vendor, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Enricher.vendorIdentifier()"},{"text":" sets on every record’s context: the one identifier that outlives","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a session that Traffluent offers, and only because the operating system owns it.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/StandardContext\/documentation\/StandardContext\/VendorIdentifierKey"},"topicSect